WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.340
- [Narrator] At the end
of the 17th century,

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.290
a woman named Jang Gye-Hyang
began a recipe book.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.510
This cookbook not only detailed dishes

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.800
eaten by Korean noblemen of the time,

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.590
but also how to store and ferment food.

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:16.360
The cookbook would go on to survive

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.460
and inspire generations of cooks

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.860
and continues to be as relevant today

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.378
in modern Korean cooking
as in the 17th century.

00:00:24.378 --> 00:00:26.961
(bright music)

00:00:28.988 --> 00:00:31.012
(somber music)

00:00:31.012 --> 00:00:34.929
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:18.327 --> 00:03:20.994
(bright music)

